            <ArticleTitle>Flux projection beamforming for monochromatic source localization in enclosed space.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>EL1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1121/1.4973193</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Monochromatic sound source localization becomes difficult in enclosed space. According to the reciprocity theorem, a self-consistent method of source localization in enclosed space, referred to as the flux projection beamforming, is proposed, only using the measurement of the sound pressure and normal velocity on the closed boundary at a single frequency. Its validity is examined both by experiment and simulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
